# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop(42) injects a return value into all sleeping strands under
#         that tag; echo of the stopped block shows the injected value.
# defer-to: M4 (requires tag.stop(val) method dispatch and ',' separator runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   tag.stop(42) is called as an urbiscript method on a UTag value — M4 object-
#   method dispatch.  urbi_tag_stop in the C API does not accept a return value
#   at M3 (the valued-stop semantic is scheduled with the full tag API in M4).
#   The fixture also uses ',' to run three sleeping blocks concurrently (M5 chk
#   driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with valued tag.stop and M5 chk driver):
# # var t = Tag.new() | {};
# # echo({t: sleep(3600s)}), echo({t: sleep(3600s)}), echo({t: sleep(3600s)}),
# # sleep(100ms); t.stop(42); sleep(100ms);
# # [00000001] *** 42
# # [00000002] *** 42
# # [00000003] *** 42
